christmas is coming early for  PlayStation 4 owners sony has sent out a  survey hinting at future features for  firmware updates including being able to  change your PSN ID and having custom  backgrounds and new face plates are set  to be released in November so maybe not  the most exciting Christmas but still  sony has sent out survey asking  PlayStation 4 users what they think are  the most important features that should  be added to the console among the  choices are much requested features such  as the ability to change a playstation  network ID custom backgrounds and the  option to hide or completely remove  items from the library function also  found on the list of options are psone  classics and ps2 classics indicating the  platform holder may be gauging the  demand for more releases the survey also  asks when respondents expect PlayStation  to release the next big system software  update with a range of timeframe  starting from before the end of 2015 and  going up to 2017 or later available to  pick the last update 3.0 was released on  sep tember 30th it added a number of  features including Twitter sharing for  videos tweaks to the interface for  streaming on YouTube and an increase in  online storage capacity from one  gigabyte to 10 gigabyte for PS plus  members the PlayStation 4 will also be  getting custom face plates in the UK and  Australia allowing players to change the  color of the top of the console the  faceplates come in six colors neon  orange aqua blue glacier white gold  silver and red the gold and silver  colors will not be available in the UK  or Ireland with the rest will launch on  November eighteenth are you planning to  buy one of the faceplates what features  would you like to see added to the  PlayStation 4 an update for point now  let us know in the comments or you can  find me on Twitter at how not to draw  i'm kate and thanks for watching
 

